diff --git a/Docs/PROTOCOL.md b/Docs/PROTOCOL.md
index 4c2d83037d4912c6f06a064149f04e6a714797a0..9755abc4d29248806f11582f1b03ced936eca6a9
--- a/Docs/PROTOCOL.md
+++ b/Docs/PROTOCOL.md
@@ -105,3 +105,47 @@
 ## Phase 1 note
 
 The Unity host implements the same messages; the Quest client replaces `site.html`. The C# port is accepted only when the headless Stage 1 transcript (`state` snapshots at each day boundary plus every `event`, `report`, `result`) matches the Node host's transcript for the same scenario and seed within the golden tolerances.
+
+## Level 1 additions (WO-L1)
+
+`rules.planControlsClock: true` allows the primary Plan connection to send `ctrl start`
+and `ctrl reset`. Other controls remain facilitator-only; mirrors remain read-only.
+The host starts paused. The opening PM line is delivered on Start, once per run.
+During an argument, Plan may only commit one `hold` for the trailing crew; other
+orders return `The field won't take that order right now` without naming the problem.
+Site may observe (`moveTo`, `mount`, `dismount`, `inspect`, `listen`), but cannot change work.
+
+For this mode, Plan's view contains `plannedLines`, `plannedPolylines` (the original
+PM plan), `reportedLines` (through yesterday), `held` (booleans keyed by crew),
+`promisedDay`, `deadlineDay`, and authored `crews` with `id`, `name`, `foreman`,
+`startDay`, `rate` (ft/day). `project` and `plan.locked` retain their meanings.
+`siteClient` is the primary Site connection's hello `client`: `quest`, `web`, or
+`null` when disconnected. `previousRun` contains the prior run's actual polylines,
+or null. These additions carry no live field positions to Plan. Reports omit money.
+Site crews add `onSite`: false before their start or while an unstarted crew is held.
+
+At the result Plan receives only `t`, `v`, `stage`, `finishDay`, `promisedDay`,
+`idleDays` (per crew), `lines` (`planned`, `actual`), and `previousRun` with the same
+public result fields. Site receives only `{t:"result",v:1,stage}`. The facilitator
+retains the full result; money remains internal to the simulation and facilitator.
+Reset retains the previous completed run for the faint chart overlay.
+
+New voice messages retain `lineIds` and add `turns`, in speaking order:
+
+```json
+{"t":"voice","v":1,"day":3.89,"lineIds":["marcus_collapse"],"seats":["site"],"turns":[{"speaker":"foreman_pipe","text":"Wall's moving! Out of the hole, everybody out, now!","clip":"marcus_collapse_1.wav","stationFt":520.2}]}
+```
+
+The host also includes the authored line objects in `lines`, including `turns` for
+exchanges. Play each `turns[].clip` from `/Voice/<stage>/`, at its speaker's crew
+position (`stationFt` is omitted for PM/radio). Do not overlap exchanges; leave
+0.3 real seconds between turns. No captions during play. PM reaches Plan only;
+foremen reach Site only. Arrivals can repeat on a new display day, at most once
+per crew per day; repeat grumbles at most once per pair per day. Other lines play
+once per run. Listen near a crew replays its last exchange.
+
+`/play.html` is the Level 1 PC page. Its Rules link serves `/level1/rules.pdf`;
+`/level1/rules.html` is also available. Existing stage pages are retained.
+With `--discovery`, the Node host sends UTF-8 `LOBOVER 1 <port> <hostname>` to UDP
+7332 every two real seconds, using the broadcast address of each non-loopback
+IPv4 interface. USB uses `adb reverse tcp:7331 tcp:7331`.
diff --git a/Docs/SCENARIO_SCHEMA.md b/Docs/SCENARIO_SCHEMA.md
index cceda58e1ca4067371e979b8583c55c7b639e747..798b2f6f3129991532b09fc178d79c2ac1ff30e3
--- a/Docs/SCENARIO_SCHEMA.md
+++ b/Docs/SCENARIO_SCHEMA.md
@@ -107,3 +107,31 @@
 | `{"kind":"result"}` | the simulation emits its result |
 
 Triggers are latched. Beats remain ordered; an unfired earlier beat is marked skipped when a later beat becomes due. A trigger reached during a paused Site trip waits until the current beat ends. Reset clears readiness, completed/skipped beats and latched triggers. Loading a different scenario disables an incompatible guide. See `PROTOCOL.md` for the message and Ready/Continue behavior.
+
+## Level 1 opt-in fields (WO-L1)
+
+Existing slice and stage scenarios omit these fields and keep their existing behavior.
+
+| Field | Effect |
+| --- | --- |
+| P1 `durationDays` | Resolves automatically at `firedT + durationDays`, without a response order. Omit to retain clearing-machine behavior. |
+| `rules.orderLag: "none"` | All orders land immediately, independent of Site position. |
+| `time.slowUntil: "eventEnd"` | Slow while an event is active or an argument remains unresolved; full otherwise. Commits do not override this. The host uses the authored `secondsPerDayFull` and `secondsPerDaySlow`. |
+| `rules.holdBeforeStartDelaysStart: true` | Holding an unstarted crew keeps it off site and unbilled. Resume (or finite hold expiry) sets its start to that moment. Already-started holds still accrue idle time. |
+| `rules.planControlsClock: true` | Plan can Start and Reset; uses the Level 1 filtered views, unchanged original plan overlay, and Hold/Go-only argument resolution. |
+
+With Plan clock control and `permits.heldBy: "pm"`, permit cards still identify
+each zone and posted number, but may omit `code`. With inspections not required,
+`inspections.cards` may be empty. `crews[].foreman` supplies the authored display name.
+
+Voice lines may have `turns: [{speaker, text}, ...]` instead of a single `speaker`
+and `text`. An exchange is nonempty and all speakers use the existing cast IDs.
+New triggers: `event` matches `eventType`; `arrive` matches `crew` and `status`
+while Site is dismounted within 30 m (at most once per crew/display day);
+`conflict` may match `pair` (`back-pipe`, `pipe-exc`) and `cause` (`leaderStopped`
+when the leader is not moving, otherwise `caughtUp`). The most specific conflict
+match wins: pair and cause, then pair, then any. `conflictRepeat` matches `pair`
+on later catch-ups, at most once per pair/display day, without another stop.
+The first argument retains the existing `crossWithinNextDay` simulation rule.
+For the new line sheet, PM/radio route to Plan, foremen to Site, and lines play
+once except the explicitly daily arrival/repeat triggers and a requested Listen replay.
diff --git a/Monitor/e2e/level1.e2e.js b/Monitor/e2e/level1.e2e.js
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..17077b5b1316919953e085cbb053f9cd21044102
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Monitor/e2e/level1.e2e.js
@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@
+import test from 'node:test';
+import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
+import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';
+import { mkdir } from 'node:fs/promises';
+import { chromium } from 'playwright';
+import { startHost } from '../src/host/server.js';
+
+const scenarioPath=fileURLToPath(new URL('../../Data/Scenarios/level1_texas.json',import.meta.url));
+const output=fileURLToPath(new URL('../out/level1/',import.meta.url));
+async function clickReply(page, selector) {
+  const response=page.evaluate(()=>new Promise(resolve=>{
+    const listener=event=>{const m=JSON.parse(event.data);if(['ack','nack'].includes(m.t)){socket.removeEventListener('message',listener);resolve(m);}};
+    socket.addEventListener('message',listener);
+  }));
+  await page.locator(selector).click();return response;
+}
+test('Level 1 page: Start, Hold, Go, result, Run again, browser Site status and argument rejection', {timeout:60000}, async () => {
+  const host=await startHost({scenarioPath,port:0,testMode:true});let browser;
+  try {
+    browser=await chromium.launch({headless:true});
+    const context=await browser.newContext({viewport:{width:1280,height:1000}});
